    GUIDE_PROFILES.james_sheldon.life = `James Sheldon Webb was born on 11 April 1943 at Snowflake, Navajo County, Arizona. The FamilySearch person-page birth entry names his father as James Wilford Webb, his mother as Marion Beulah Brenay, and certificate number 793. The indexed citation is internally consistent with the immediate Webb household; the original certificate image remains a separate preservation target.

His early years unfolded in Arizona during the Second World War and the hard postwar years that followed. Family testimony describes the Webb household near the mill as modest and mobile, with a one-room shack, a lean-to kitchen, heavy snow, and a long walk to the family car. When Jay entered Army service, Marion carried the household through separation, limited money, and Sheldon’s serious childhood illness. The family memories are retained as testimony and are clearly distinguished from civil-record facts.

The captured FamilySearch visual record now follows Sheldon from infancy through adulthood: a baby portrait, fourth-birthday image, Vernon school photographs, sixth-, seventh-, eighth-, and probable ninth-grade portraits, high-school and graduation material, and photographs of the Webb children at home. The 1950 Apache County census image places seven-year-old James S. Webb in the household of James W. Webb and Marion B. Webb. Family photographs add the Webbville home, timber and White Mountains work, the Hawkins–Webb kin network, rural household life, and later family gatherings.

The military record is represented by Air Force training and uniform portraits and by the attached Veterans Affairs BIRLS citation. Family testimony says Sheldon served roughly two and a half years and received a hardship discharge so he could help his father; the exact unit, service dates, and discharge document remain open targets. He and Inez Karen Prather attended college together, and the 1968 Northern Arizona University graduation announcement and sibling-graduation clipping preserve that educational chapter.

The 1965 engagement announcement, Mesa Temple wedding photographs, county-marriage citation, reception photograph, and later family portraits document Sheldon’s marriage to Inez and the growth of their household. Additional captured documents preserve the family’s 1980 sealing, Sheldon’s participation in Aaron’s airport welcome, and his four-page life sketch for Uncle Joe Brenay. That life sketch is especially important because it shows Sheldon acting as a keeper and presenter of family history, not merely appearing in it.

Sheldon died on 9 April 2016 in Gilbert, Maricopa County, Arizona, and is associated with Lakeside Cemetery in Lakeside, Navajo County. His later record combines a page-level birth citation, the original 1950 census image, attached marriage and military-source metadata, and a large body of captioned family photographs and documents. Where the underlying source image was not preserved, that limitation remains stated rather than concealed.`;
